\PYG{c+cm}{/*}
\PYG{c+cm}{   DYNAMIC CONVEX HULL TRICK (LINE CONTAINER }
\PYG{c+cm}{   Idea:}
\PYG{c+cm}{   \PYGZhy{} Maintains the upper envelope of a set of lines y = k*x + m.}
\PYG{c+cm}{   \PYGZhy{} Allows dynamically adding lines and querying the MAXIMUM y value at }
\PYG{c+cm}{     a given x in O(log N) time.}
\PYG{c+cm}{   \PYGZhy{} For MINIMUM queries: insert(\PYGZhy{}k, \PYGZhy{}m) and negate the query result: \PYGZhy{}query(x).}
\PYG{c+cm}{   How it works (KACTL approach):}
\PYG{c+cm}{   \PYGZhy{} Uses std::multiset to keep lines sorted by slope \PYGZsq{}k\PYGZsq{}.}
\PYG{c+cm}{   \PYGZhy{} Maintains the intersection point \PYGZsq{}p\PYGZsq{} with the next line.}
\PYG{c+cm}{   \PYGZhy{} Uses C++14 heterogeneous lookup (less\PYGZlt{}\PYGZgt{}) to binary search by \PYGZsq{}x\PYGZsq{} value }
\PYG{c+cm}{     using the \PYGZsq{}p\PYGZsq{} attribute.}
\PYG{c+cm}{   Complexity:}
\PYG{c+cm}{   \PYGZhy{} Add line: Amortized O(log N)}
\PYG{c+cm}{   \PYGZhy{} Query: O(log N)}
\PYG{c+cm}{*/}
